  "prefLabel": "Rev 1804.06 Appeal",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 1804.06 Appeal. If the municipal assessing officials neglect or refuse to abate the inconsistent use penalty, a property owner may either:\n\n(a) Apply in writing, accompanied by the required fee, to the New Hampshire board of tax and land appeals within 240 days of the date of tax notice pursuant to RSA 79-B:5; or\n\n(b) Petition the New Hampshire superior court in the county where the property is located within 240 days of the date of tax notice pursuant to RSA 79-B:5.\n\nSource. #8567, eff 2-14-06; ss by #10560, eff 3-28-14; ss by #13867, eff 2-8-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev1800.html"
